====================================================================================
(1) prod_{i<j}(x_i-x_j) = sum_T sgn(T) x^{score(T)} -- verify + which scores survive
====================================================================================
 n=3: #tournaments=8  distinct scores hit=7  survive(coeff!=0)=6
    sum_T sgn x^score == Vandermonde exactly: True
    every surviving score is a permutation of (0..2): True
    every surviving coeff is +-1: True
 n=4: #tournaments=64  distinct scores hit=38  survive(coeff!=0)=24
    sum_T sgn x^score == Vandermonde exactly: True
    every surviving score is a permutation of (0..3): True
    every surviving coeff is +-1: True
 n=5: #tournaments=1024  distinct scores hit=291  survive(coeff!=0)=120
    sum_T sgn x^score == Vandermonde exactly: True
    every surviving score is a permutation of (0..4): True
    every surviving coeff is +-1: True

====================================================================================
(2) SURVIVAL = TRANSITIVITY: score is a permutation <=> tournament is transitive
====================================================================================
 n=4: (transitive <=> distinct scores = permutation of 0..3) for ALL tournaments: True
 n=5: (transitive <=> distinct scores = permutation of 0..4) for ALL tournaments: True
   => the surviving (uncancelled) tournaments are EXACTLY the transitive ones;
      intransitive (3-cycle-bearing) tournaments all cancel.

====================================================================================
(3) THE CANCELLING INVOLUTION: reverse the lex-first directed 3-cycle
====================================================================================
 n=4: 3-cycle reversal preserves score: True;  flips sign: True
 n=5: 3-cycle reversal preserves score: True;  flips sign: True

   Reversing a directed 3-cycle preserves every score (each cycle vertex keeps 1 win/1 loss
   inside the triangle) and flips the sign (3 arcs reverse -> parity of #upsets flips).  So it
   pairs each intransitive tournament with an opposite-signed same-score partner: THE
   INTRANSITIVE TERMS CANCEL, leaving only the transitive ones -- the Vandermonde.

